282
00:15:38,037 --> 00:15:39,497
All I see is you.

283
00:15:42,697 --> 00:16:01,857
So I have a really hard time seeing the...

284
00:16:01,857 --> 00:16:12,317
I just went and talked with the teacher.

285
00:16:15,317 --> 00:16:15,877
Huh?

286
00:16:18,157 --> 00:16:18,677
Oh.

287
00:16:19,417 --> 00:16:21,317
So he just couldn't see the board, then.

288
00:16:21,857 --> 00:16:22,277
Uh-huh.

289
00:16:22,617 --> 00:16:24,277
But that's all taken care of now.

290
00:16:25,057 --> 00:16:27,157
Why's it gotta be like this?

291
00:16:27,157 --> 00:16:29,157
In the worst way possible, but...

292
00:16:30,377 --> 00:16:30,877
Sorry.

293
00:16:31,577 --> 00:16:31,917
No.

294
00:16:32,217 --> 00:16:33,377
I know you...

295
00:16:33,377 --> 00:16:35,397
Have plenty to worry about already.

296
00:16:36,017 --> 00:16:36,177
Hm?

297
00:16:36,657 --> 00:16:37,437
What exactly?

298
00:16:37,957 --> 00:16:38,197
Huh?

299
00:16:38,737 --> 00:16:39,777
You know, like...

300
00:16:39,777 --> 00:16:41,257
That big movie and stuff?

301
00:16:41,697 --> 00:16:41,857
Hm?

302
00:16:42,577 --> 00:16:44,637
Are you into watching movies, Ishikawa?

303
00:16:44,997 --> 00:16:47,077
It's like she was waiting for me to bring it up.

304
00:16:47,237 --> 00:16:49,897
Um, so you're gonna be in one with a real director?

305
00:16:50,837 --> 00:16:51,237
Yep.

306
00:16:51,597 --> 00:16:52,417
Sure am.

307
00:16:52,717 --> 00:16:53,557
Playing a tree?

308
00:16:53,557 --> 00:16:54,357
What?

309
00:16:54,857 --> 00:16:55,557
Be for real.

310
00:16:55,957 --> 00:16:58,637
I play the daughter of the police officer who's after the lead guy.

311
00:16:59,097 --> 00:17:00,337
And it's a real role, too.

312
00:17:01,117 --> 00:17:01,537
Oh.

313
00:17:01,877 --> 00:17:02,697
Is that all?

314
00:17:03,677 --> 00:17:08,517
She's a high school student, and her police officer dad dies partway through it, but...

315
00:17:08,517 --> 00:17:08,817
Wait.

316
00:17:09,297 --> 00:17:11,517
She seems way more excited than earlier.

317
00:17:12,177 --> 00:17:13,557
Was it because...

318
00:17:13,557 --> 00:17:15,777
No one bothered to ask her about her part?

319
00:17:16,457 --> 00:17:18,097
I even have a real line!

320
00:17:18,437 --> 00:17:18,777
Huh.

321
00:17:19,437 --> 00:17:20,357
Ahem.

322
00:17:20,357 --> 00:17:25,397
You're such a creep.

323
00:17:25,817 --> 00:17:26,077
Huh?

324
00:17:28,877 --> 00:17:30,357
That's my whole big line.

325
00:17:30,997 --> 00:17:31,757
Uh-oh.

326
00:17:32,397 --> 00:17:33,437
Big line, huh?

327
00:17:34,077 --> 00:17:37,097
I don't usually talk like that, so I need to practice.

328
00:17:38,557 --> 00:17:38,957
Ugh.

329
00:17:40,417 --> 00:17:41,737
You're such a creep.

330
00:17:42,817 --> 00:17:44,757
You should sound even more serious.

331
00:17:45,377 --> 00:17:46,717
You're such a creep.

332
00:17:47,057 --> 00:17:47,497
Oh, yeah.

333
00:17:47,857 --> 00:17:48,477
That's good.

334
00:17:48,777 --> 00:17:49,917
You're such a creep.

335
00:17:49,917 --> 00:17:50,937
That's even better.

336
00:17:51,717 --> 00:17:52,717
You're such a creep.

337
00:17:52,857 --> 00:17:54,017
You're getting better and better.

338
00:17:54,197 --> 00:17:54,497
Wow.

339
00:17:56,037 --> 00:17:56,597
Wait.

340
00:17:57,017 --> 00:17:57,397
Hang on.

341
00:17:57,717 --> 00:17:59,577
We should really go somewhere that's less crowded.

342
00:17:59,797 --> 00:18:00,437
She's dangerous.

343
00:18:02,837 --> 00:18:05,677
For what you need, isn't this a little too private?

344
00:18:06,057 --> 00:18:08,597
It's not like there's anywhere else we can go.

345
00:18:08,977 --> 00:18:09,377
Maybe.

346
00:18:09,757 --> 00:18:11,857
But this is pretty cramped for the two of us.

347
00:18:12,377 --> 00:18:12,937
Mm-hmm.

348
00:18:12,937 --> 00:18:18,137
So, well, uh, when's the movie actually coming out?

349
00:18:18,357 --> 00:18:20,357
We start filming relatively soon.

350
00:18:20,577 --> 00:18:22,197
Maybe springtime two years from now?

351
00:18:22,717 --> 00:18:24,417
That's a long ways off.

352
00:18:24,757 --> 00:18:25,977
That's just how it goes.

353
00:18:26,797 --> 00:18:28,637
Spring two years from now.

354
00:18:28,637 --> 00:18:37,517
So, by then, will me and her still be together?

355
00:18:40,157 --> 00:18:41,417
Will you go see it?

356
00:18:41,417 --> 00:18:43,217
I don't know.

357
00:18:43,717 --> 00:18:44,217
What?

358
00:18:44,837 --> 00:18:47,237
But I'll see what all I can manage.

359
00:18:47,717 --> 00:18:49,197
What's that supposed to mean?

360
00:18:51,437 --> 00:18:56,557
I'll see if I can go see it.

361
00:18:56,557 --> 00:19:08,237
Then we're done.

362
00:19:08,697 --> 00:19:08,957
Huh?

363
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:11,757
What about practicing your lines?

364
00:19:16,337 --> 00:19:17,797
I can't say that.

365
00:19:17,797 --> 00:19:32,757
Discovery Columbus Gakuin!

366
00:19:33,757 --> 00:19:34,397
Huh?

367
00:19:34,957 --> 00:19:35,777
Here goes.

368
00:19:36,857 --> 00:19:37,997
Here we are, everyone.

369
00:19:38,237 --> 00:19:40,757
It's Discovery Columbus Gakuin!

370
00:19:41,577 --> 00:19:41,917
What?

371
00:19:42,257 --> 00:19:42,817
Where is she?

372
00:19:42,817 --> 00:19:46,317
We're trying high school students to hear what the youth of today have to say.

373
00:19:46,317 --> 00:19:47,257
Should prove everything...

374
00:19:47,257 --> 00:19:47,857
There she is!

375
00:19:48,157 --> 00:19:49,777
Here's our topic for the day.

376
00:19:50,217 --> 00:19:51,837
She's wearing a sailor uniform.

377
00:19:52,117 --> 00:19:52,657
Let's talk about Shumai.

378
00:19:52,917 --> 00:19:54,437
Do you like Shumai, Mai Mai?

379
00:19:54,797 --> 00:19:55,917
I love Shumai!

380
00:19:56,237 --> 00:19:57,417
Mai Mai, yes, I do!

381
00:19:58,357 --> 00:19:59,617
Was that it?

382
00:20:00,037 --> 00:20:02,277
Guess it's hard to get air time with so many people.

383
00:20:03,237 --> 00:20:03,757
Terrific.

384
00:20:04,177 --> 00:20:06,257
Now then, let's hear from Miku.

385
00:20:06,457 --> 00:20:06,677
Oh!

386
00:20:06,937 --> 00:20:09,937
Does anyone really want apricot placed in their lunchbox?

387
00:20:10,177 --> 00:20:10,497
What?

388
00:20:10,497 --> 00:20:11,917
Of course they do!

389
00:20:12,237 --> 00:20:13,457
Look at her, looking at her!

390
00:20:14,537 --> 00:20:15,777
She's gonna say something!

391
00:20:15,777 --> 00:20:16,997
All right, students.

392
00:20:17,097 --> 00:20:17,757
Thanks for answering.

393
00:20:17,977 --> 00:20:19,417
We've got all your opinions in.

394
00:20:19,797 --> 00:20:20,037
What?

395
00:20:20,897 --> 00:20:21,597
Don't tell me.

396
00:20:21,617 --> 00:20:22,717
Well, there you have it, folks.

397
00:20:22,737 --> 00:20:23,377
She's on again!

398
00:20:23,417 --> 00:20:25,237
Right out of the mouths of the kids themselves.

399
00:20:25,237 --> 00:20:25,597
No, wait.

400
00:20:25,817 --> 00:20:28,137
I wouldn't believe it if I heard it myself.

401
00:20:28,677 --> 00:20:29,557
But now you know...

402
00:20:29,557 --> 00:20:30,957
This probably happens all the time.

403
00:20:31,097 --> 00:20:32,097
This is how the youth of today really...

404
00:20:32,097 --> 00:20:35,197
She's really only on when she's staring at someone too much.

405
00:20:35,897 --> 00:20:38,797
Or laughing at the comedian's really unfunny jokes.

406
00:20:40,277 --> 00:20:42,197
Or when she doesn't fit in her box.

407
00:20:42,477 --> 00:20:44,617
Be sure to tune in again next week.

408
00:20:44,617 --> 00:20:47,657
And the whole episode ends without her saying a thing.

409
00:20:49,137 --> 00:20:49,877
So why...

410
00:20:51,057 --> 00:20:54,377
Why do I feel so relieved?

411
00:20:56,877 --> 00:20:57,917
I'm the worst.

412
00:20:58,837 --> 00:21:01,457
She's probably so upset right now.

413
00:21:07,137 --> 00:21:08,677
Best try not to bring it up.

414
00:21:08,677 --> 00:21:12,357
Did you watch me last night?

415
00:21:12,557 --> 00:21:14,177
I got a lot of screen time.

416
00:21:14,517 --> 00:21:15,897
She was fine with that?

417
00:21:16,177 --> 00:21:17,257
I guess you were on a bit.

418
00:21:17,817 --> 00:21:20,557
Yamada's got a long way to go before she's a famous actress.

419
00:21:21,557 --> 00:21:22,297
Oh, and here.

420
00:21:22,797 --> 00:21:23,557
What's this?

421
00:21:24,297 --> 00:21:25,077
Can't you tell?

422
00:21:25,197 --> 00:21:26,377
Naoki Suga's signature.

423
00:21:26,977 --> 00:21:27,837
This is fake!

424
00:21:28,897 --> 00:21:31,257
A long, long way.

425
00:21:31,257 --> 00:21:33,537
Why did you even think this would work?

